WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.236 --> 00:00:01.720
(light music)

00:00:01.720 --> 00:00:03.540
- [Jamie Hall] As we look ahead
to an all electric future,

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:06.206
we really talk about not
leaving anyone behind.

00:00:06.206 --> 00:00:09.320
(light music)

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:11.120
- The San Joaquin Valley in California.

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:13.130
It has some major challenges.

00:00:13.130 --> 00:00:16.040
It's got some of the most severe poverty

00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:19.044
and the worst air quality
in the entire United States.

00:00:19.044 --> 00:00:20.640
(light music)

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:22.200
- The transportation industry

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:23.990
is really at an inflection point.

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:25.770
We've got to fundamentally transform

00:00:25.770 --> 00:00:27.340
this whole sector of the economy.

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:29.450
And this particularly
includes the communities

00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:31.504
that are hardest hit by climate change.

00:00:31.504 --> 00:00:33.810
(light music)

00:00:33.810 --> 00:00:36.040
- What Valley Clean Air Now is looking at

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:38.260
is how we bring climate equity

00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:39.960
to the places that need it most.

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:42.737
- There's a lot of need and
people rely on these vehicles.

00:00:42.737 --> 00:00:44.180
(light music)

00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:45.410
- [Tom Knox] At our event here today,

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:47.130
we've got hundreds of people

00:00:47.130 --> 00:00:50.230
who need help with their small repairs.

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:51.700
When we look at transitioning

00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:53.180
into an electric vehicle future,

00:00:53.180 --> 00:00:56.641
it's important to remember,
it's not there for everyone yet.

00:00:56.641 --> 00:00:59.558
(speaking Spanish)

00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:04.900
- The older, the vehicle,

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:06.460
the higher the emissions are going to be.

00:01:06.460 --> 00:01:09.890
So we've offered them $850 in repairs,

00:01:09.890 --> 00:01:12.677
which typically fixes the vehicle.

00:01:12.677 --> 00:01:15.594
(speaking Spanish)

00:01:20.120 --> 00:01:22.010
- [Tom Knox] We're also going
to educate them on the fact

00:01:22.010 --> 00:01:25.530
that we can help them
replace their older vehicle

00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:27.525
with a used electric vehicle.

00:01:27.525 --> 00:01:29.240
(light music)

00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:31.050
- [Jamie Hall] We need to
figure out how to do this

00:01:31.050 --> 00:01:33.210
in a way that provides
benefits for everyone.

00:01:33.210 --> 00:01:35.281
And doesn't leave anyone behind.

00:01:35.281 --> 00:01:37.970
(light music)

00:01:37.970 --> 00:01:39.620
- Right now for electric vehicles,

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:42.290
they're so new that we don't have enough

00:01:42.290 --> 00:01:44.793
electric vehicle
technicians out there yet.

00:01:45.980 --> 00:01:47.740
- I've always wanted to learn this.

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:49.023
It's the future for me.

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:52.750
- [Tom Knox] The only way
to create those technicians

00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:56.740
are really passionate expert instructors.

00:01:56.740 --> 00:01:59.190
- When the opportunity arose
to work with Valley CAN

00:01:59.190 --> 00:02:02.113
in order to develop this
training, it was a no-brainer.

00:02:03.130 --> 00:02:05.480
One of my passions is
helping students transition

00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:08.110
from education into the workforce.

00:02:08.110 --> 00:02:09.850
- The market is growing quickly.

00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:11.520
We need to really grow the pool of people

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:12.960
who have the skills and knowledge

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:14.820
to work on electric vehicles.

00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:16.430
- I feel like this class is going to be

00:02:16.430 --> 00:02:17.840
a solution to a big problem.

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:19.640
The change is going to happen fast,

00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:22.170
and it's exciting that I'm
getting my foot in the door

00:02:22.170 --> 00:02:24.100
to learn about that change.

00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:25.990
- There's this mentality
out there that I've noticed

00:02:25.990 --> 00:02:30.390
where it's almost like people
consider these to be UFO's.

00:02:30.390 --> 00:02:31.710
They're still vehicles.

00:02:31.710 --> 00:02:33.730
It's all stuff that's held
together with nuts and bolts.

00:02:33.730 --> 00:02:36.380
It's just the technology that propels it

00:02:36.380 --> 00:02:39.020
down the road is different.

00:02:39.020 --> 00:02:41.630
- Having this class means a lot, you know.

00:02:41.630 --> 00:02:44.330
It gives me an edge in
this growing industry.

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:46.410
It's going to help myself and my family.

00:02:46.410 --> 00:02:48.740
- This is no longer car mechanics

00:02:48.740 --> 00:02:50.600
as we used to think of it.

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:53.120
This is more a technology job.

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:56.570
This new generation of
electric vehicle technicians

00:02:56.570 --> 00:03:00.440
in 5 or 10 years, they've got
enormous career opportunities.

00:03:00.440 --> 00:03:02.070
They are going to be
the hands-on innovators

00:03:02.070 --> 00:03:04.940
that really make electric
vehicles work for America.

00:03:04.940 --> 00:03:06.240
- There is an opportunity out there

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:07.260
if you're willing to take it.

00:03:07.260 --> 00:03:11.450
And doors will open up if
you're willing to take a chance.

00:03:11.450 --> 00:03:13.222
I want to be a part of that change.

00:03:13.222 --> 00:03:15.722
(light music)

